            <ArticleTitle>Role of leukotriene receptor antagonists in the treatment of exercise-induced bronchoconstriction: a review.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>60-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1186/1710-1492-1-2-60</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Asthma is a very common disorder that still causes significant morbidity and mortality. A high percentage of individuals with asthma also experience exercise-induced bronchoconstriction (EIB). This article reviews the current literature and updates the reader on the safety, efficacy, and clinical applications of leukotriene modifiers in the treatment of EIB.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
